                %li
                  %a{:href => "#hilbert_schemes_and_higgscoulomb_branches"} Hilbert schemes and Higgs/Coulomb branches
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Hilbert schemes are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli spaces
            of subvarieties, hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+%28mathematics%29"} configuration spaces
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
          %p
            For instance a scheme of 0-dimensional sub-schemes is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+scheme+of+points"} Hilbert scheme of points
          %p
            Specifically for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+variety"} quasi-projective variety
            with fixed
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Hilbert polynomial
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Hilbert+polynomial"} ?
          %p The existence and construction of Hilbert schemes is due to Grothendieck (FGA).
          %p
            The Hilbert scheme of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^2
            is widely studied in combinatorics and geometric representation theory for its connections to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Macdonald+polynomials"} Macdonald polynomials
            and
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cherednik+algebra"} Cherednik algebra
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#compact_hyperkhler_structure Compact hyperkähler structure
          %p
            The only known examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+schemes+of+points"} Hilbert schemes of points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{[n+1]}
            (for
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            either
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-torus"} 4-torus
                (in which case the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
                is really the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕋
                          %mn 4
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕋
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{T}^4)^{[n]} \to \mathbb{T}^4
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Beauville83"}> Beauville 83
            ) and two exceptional examples (
            %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#OGrady99"}> O’Grady 99
            ,
            %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#OGrady03"} O’Grady 03
            ), see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Sawon04"} Sawon 04, Sec. 5.3
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+of+rational+maps"} homotopy of rational maps
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%A1nos+Koll%C3%A1r"}> János Kollár
              , Chapter I of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Rational Curves on Algebraic Varieties
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 32
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-03276-3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-03276-3
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilbert_scheme"} Hilbert scheme
          %h3#hilbert_schemes_of_points Hilbert schemes of points
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiraku+Nakajima"}> Hiraku Nakajima
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Hilbert schemes of points on surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/ulect-18"} ams:ulect-18
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiraku+Nakajima"}> Hiraku Nakajima
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em More lectures on Hilbert schemes of points on surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.6782"} arXiv:1401.6782
            %li
              %p
                J. Bertin,
                %em The punctual Hilbert scheme: An introduction
                (
                %a{:href => "https://www-fourier.ujf-grenoble.fr/sites/ifmaquette.ujf-grenoble.fr/files/bertin_rev.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                Dori Bejleri,
                %em Hilbert schemes: Geometry, combionatorics, and representation theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.harvard.edu/~bejleri/Hilbertschemes_gss.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                Barbara Bolognese, Ivan Losev,
                %em A general introduction to the Hilbert scheme of points on the plane
                (
                %a{:href => "https://web.northeastern.edu/iloseu/Barbara_14_complete.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                Joachim Jelisiejew,
                %em Pathologies on the Hilbert scheme of points
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.08531"}> arXiv:1812.08531
                )
          %p
            Discussion in relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+compactifications"} Fulton-MacPherson compactifications
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
          %ul
            %li#FultonMacPherson94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Fulton"}> William Fulton
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+MacPherson"} Robert MacPherson
              = succeed "," do
                %em A compactification of configuration spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2946631"} jstor:2946631
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+numbers"} Euler numbers
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+schemes+of+points"} Hilbert schemes of points
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiraku+Nakajima"}> Hiraku Nakajima
              ,
              %em Euler numbers of Hilbert schemes of points on simple surface singularities and quantum dimensions of standard modules of quantum affine algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.03834"}> arXiv:2001.03834
              )
          %h3#as_moduli_spaces_of_instantons As moduli spaces of instantons
          %p
            Discussion in their role as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Sean Pohorence,
                %em Hilbert scheme of points and the ADHM construction
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.ihes.fr/~celliott/Hilbert_Schemes_of_Points.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/PohorenceHilbertScheme.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ian+Grojnowski"}> Ian Grojnowski
                ,
                %em Instantons and affine algebras I: The Hilbert scheme and vertex operators
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9506020"}> arXiv:alg-geom/9506020
                )
          %p
            Specifically in relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donaldson-Thomas+theory"} Donaldson-Thomas theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Michele Cirafici, Annamaria Sinkovics,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cohomological gauge theory, quiver matrix models and Donaldson-Thomas theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0803.4188"} arXiv:0803.4188
            %li
              %p
                Artan Sheshmani,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hilbert Schemes, Donaldson-Thomas theory, Vafa-Witten and Seiberg-Witten theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://j.mp/2U7qd01"} j.mp:2U7qd01
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://scholar.harvard.edu/files/artan/files/iccm_07_02_a03.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Artan Sheshmani,
                %em Hilbert Schemes, Donaldson-Thomas Theory, Vafa-Witten and Seiberg Witten theories
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.01796"}> arxiv:1911.01796
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Jian Zhou,
              %em K-Theory of Hilbert Schemes as a Formal Quantum Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.06080"}> arXiv:1803.06080
              )
          %h3#of_ade_singularities Of ADE singularities
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+schemes+of+points"} Hilbert schemes of points
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularities"} ADE-singularities
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenji+Mohri"}> Kenji Mohri
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kähler Moduli Space of a D-Brane at Orbifold Singularities
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9806052"} arXiv:hep-th/9806052
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ron+Donagi"}> Ron Donagi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheldon+Katz"} Sheldon Katz
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Sharpe"} Eric Sharpe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spectra of D-branes with Higgs vevs
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0309270"} arXiv:hep-th/0309270
            %li
              %p
                D. Maulik, A. Oblomkov,
                = succeed "n-resolutions_," do
                  %em Quantum cohomology of the Hilbert scheme of points on A
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0802.2737"} arXiv:0802.2737
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Yukari Ito,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiraku+Nakajima"} Hiraku Nakajima
              %em McKay correspondence and Hilbert schemes in dimension three
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9803120"}> math/9803120
              )
          %h3#of_k3_surfaces Of K3 surfaces
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+schemes+of+points"} Hilbert schemes of points
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surfaces"} K3-surfaces
          %ul
            %li#Beauville83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Beauville"}> Arnaud Beauville
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Variétés Kähleriennes dont la premiere classe de Chern est nulle
              %p
                Diff. Geom. 18 (1983), 755–782 (
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214438181"}> euclid.jdg/1214438181
                )
            %li
              %p
                Georg Oberdieck,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gromov-Witten invariants of the Hilbert schemes of points of a K3 surface
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.1139"} arXiv:1406.1139
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/OberdieckK3HilbertSchemes.pdf", :title => "thesis pdf"} thesis pdf
              %p
                (using
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+invariants"} Gromov-Witten invariants
          %p
            Discussion of configuration spaces of
            %em possibly coincident
            points on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surfaces"} K3-surfaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+products"} symmetric products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^n/Sym(n)
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-D4-brane+bound+states"} D0-D4-brane bound states
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapped
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surfaces"} K3-surfaces
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"}> Cumrun Vafa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Strong Coupling Test of S-Duality
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9408074"} arXiv:hep-th/9408074
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"}> Cumrun Vafa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Instantons on D-branes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9512078"} arXiv:hep-th/9512078
          %p
            Suggestion that this is to be resolved by the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+scheme+of+points"} Hilbert scheme of points
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Harvey"}> Jeffrey Harvey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the algebras of BPS states
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9609017"} arXiv:hep-th/9609017
            %li
              %p
                Kazuyuki Furuuchi, Hiroshi Kunitomo, Toshio Nakatsu, p. 17 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological Field Theory and Second-Quantized Five-Branes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9610016"} arXiv:hep-th/9610016
          %p
            Hilbert schemes on K3 as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+vector+bundles"} stable vector bundles
          %ul
            %li
              Laura Costa Farràs,
              = succeed "," do
                %em K3 surfaces: moduli spaces and Hilbert schemes
              %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/2445/16925"} hdl:2445/16925
          %p
            with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+theory"} Rozansky-Witten theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"}> ground field
            \-valued
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+weight+systems"} Rozansky-Witten weight systems
          %ul
            %li#RobertsWillerton06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Roberts"}> Justin Roberts
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Willerton"} Simon Willerton
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Rozansky-Witten weight systems
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0602653"} arXiv:math/0602653
            %li#Sawon04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Sawon"}> Justin Sawon
                , Section 5.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rozansky-Witten invariants of hyperkähler manifold
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404360"} arXiv:math/0404360
          %h3#hilbert_schemes_and_higgscoulomb_branches Hilbert schemes and Higgs/Coulomb branches
          %p
            Identification of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+branches"} Higgs branches
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coulomb+branches"} Coulomb branches
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D3+N%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=3 N=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+schemes+of+points"} Hilbert schemes of points
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+curves"} complex curves
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+de+Boer"}> Jan de Boer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kentaro+Hori"} Kentaro Hori
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"} Hirosi Ooguri
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yaron+Oz"} Yaron Oz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mirror Symmetry in Three-Dimensional Gauge Theories, Quivers and D-branes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9611063"} arXiv:hep-th/9611063
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+de+Boer"}> Jan de Boer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kentaro+Hori"} Kentaro Hori
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"} Hirosi Ooguri
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yaron+Oz"} Yaron Oz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Mirror Symmetry in Three-Dimensional Gauge Theories,
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2,\mathbb{Z})
                    and D-Brane Moduli Spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9612131"} arXiv:hep-th/9612131
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefano+Cremonesi"}> Stefano Cremonesi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amihay+Hanany"} Amihay Hanany
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Zaffaroni"} Alberto Zaffaroni
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Monopole operators and Hilbert series of Coulomb branches of 3d
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒩
                          %mo =
                          %mn 4
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 4
                    gauge theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.2657"} arXiv:1309.2657
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Braverman"}> Alexander Braverman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Finkelberg"} Michael Finkelberg
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiraku+Nakajima"} Hiraku Nakajima
                %em Line bundles over Coulomb branches
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.11826"}> arXiv:1805.11826
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ben+Webster"}> Ben Webster
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Coherent sheaves on Hilbert schemes through the Coulomb lens
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/WebsterHilbertScheme18.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Mykola Dedushenko, Yale Fan, Silviu Pufu, Ran Yacoby, Section E.2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Coulomb Branch Quantization and Abelianized Monopole Bubbling
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.08788"} arXiv:1812.08788
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+indices"} Witten indices
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theoretic
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enumerative+geometry"} enumerative geometry
          %ul
